/*
===============================================================
EV BATTERY MONITOR — SINGLE ESP32, EVERYTHING ON ONE BOARD
===============================================================
Merges the two-board design (sensor node + compute/MQTT gateway)
back onto one chip now that the INMP441 (the reason for a second
ESP32 — I2S/ADC conflict) is gone.

What this board does:
  - Reads cell voltages through an ADS1115 (I2C) — not the
    ESP32's own ADC, so it is not affected by ADC drift/noise.
  - Reads DS18B20 cell temperatures (OneWire).
  - Reads current (ACS712), ambient temp/humidity (DHT11),
    piezo swelling sensors, and gas level — all on the ESP32's
    own ADC.
  - Runs the MOSFET PWM load control loop (LOAD/STOP commands).
  - Runs a PWM cooling fan driven by cell temperature.
  - Calculates every battery parameter locally: SOC, SOH, RUL,
    power, cell imbalance, thermal gradient, dT/dt, R0 estimate,
    SOE/SOF/SOP, power limits, energy throughput, equivalent
    cycles, time-to-empty/full.
  - Connects to WiFi/MQTT and publishes everything.
  - Prints the full sensor + parameter state to Serial every
    second, UNCONDITIONALLY — this never stops just because
    WiFi/MQTT is down. MQTT connect/retry/fail messages print
    alongside it, not instead of it.

IMPORTANT PIN NOTE: with WiFi now running on this chip, the gas
sensor was moved off GPIO25 to GPIO34. GPIO25 is an ADC2 pin,
and the ESP32's ADC2 bank is shared with the WiFi radio — reads
on it become unreliable whenever WiFi is active. GPIO34 is ADC1,
which is unaffected by WiFi. GPIO25 is reused for the fan PWM
output instead, which is fine: a digital PWM output doesn't
care about the ADC1/ADC2 split, only analogRead() does.

Sensor isolation: DS18B20 (OneWire) and the ADC reads are still
sequenced with a settle delay (temperature read ALONE, then a
wait, then current/other ADC reads) — this is carried over from
the original debugging fix for the OneWire/ADC noise-coupling
issue, and still applies even on one chip, because the problem
was electrical (supply-rail disturbance during an OneWire
transaction), not a two-chip software issue.

---------------------------------------------------------------
REV B additions (everything above is unchanged):
  * EDGE AI - the trained XGBoost health model (health_model.h,
    generated by export_model_to_c.py on the laptop) runs ON THIS
    CHIP. At the end of every discharge of 5 min or longer it
    estimates state of health from mean cell voltage, mean cell
    temperature and cycle count, explains the estimate (SHAP) and
    publishes to battery/ai_edge. No laptop or cloud needed.
  * DEMO MODE (battery/cmd/sys "DEMO_ON" / "DEMO_OFF") - the board
    stops publishing its own readings and instead runs its on-chip
    AI on the NASA replay coming from the laptop. Sent automatically
    by demo_nasa_replay.py / fake_publisher.py. Ends by itself if the
    laptop stops sending for 30 s. Load is forced off in demo mode.
  * TWO-WAY CONTROL from the digital twin:
      LIMIT:<amps>   cap the load current (twin sends this on a
                     resistance jump), LIMIT:OFF removes the cap
      FAN:<0-100>    fan duty override in %, FAN:AUTO = temperature curve
      SYNC           reset SOC from resting cell voltage (OCV table)
  * Coulomb counting uses the MEASURED time between readings. The
    loop takes longer than 1 s (the DS18B20 conversion alone is up to
    750 ms), so assuming exactly 1 s under-counted charge.
  * safety_active / safety_reason / current_limit_A / fan_mode /
    demo_mode added to the published JSON.

CHECK BEFORE TRUSTING CURRENT: ACS712_SENS_V_PER_A must match the
module printed on your ACS712 chip: 5A = 0.185, 20A = 0.100,
30A = 0.066 (current value). A mismatch scales every current reading.
---------------------------------------------------------------

Board: ESP32 Dev Module (or ESP32-S3)
Baud: 115200
Libraries needed: DHT sensor library, OneWire, DallasTemperature,
                   Adafruit_ADS1X15, WiFi, PubSubClient, ArduinoJson
FOLDER: keep health_model.h in this sketch folder (EV_SINGLE_ESP32).
===============================================================
*/

